# computer-control MCP. The lockfile is a full cross-platform freeze — always
# compile with --universal (the platform's dependency-regen runbook keys on
# this phrase). PyAutoGUI needs a DIFFERENT backend per OS (pyobjc on macOS,
# python3-xlib on Linux, pywin32 on Windows) and the satellite installs this
# MCP from requirements.txt on whichever OS the controlled machine runs, so
# the freeze carries every backend behind environment markers — the same
# pattern as satellite/requirements.txt. A plain (Linux-flavored) compile
# hard-pins the Linux backend, drops the others, and breaks macOS/Windows
# installs.
